WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.770
Since it's been so long since we saw these
characters on screen, even hardcore fans might

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.960
need a refresher course before heading to
the theater for their new adventure.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:11.600
But don't worry we've got you covered with
this look at everything you need to know before

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.500
you grab your tickets for Toy Story 4.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.000
Toy Story just wouldn't be what it is without
its two leads, so of course Tom Hanks is back

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.380
as Woody, and Tim Allen returns as Buzz Lightyear.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.999
But it isn't just those two that help give
so much heart to the world of Toy Story and

00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:27.390
luckily, just about every character in the
Toy Story universe is coming back for the

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.040
fourth film.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.960
But there are plenty of new characters to
look forward to as well.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.489
Like an overstuffed toy box, it seems there's
always room for some new characters for us

00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:35.520
to fall in love with.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.820
A huge part of the narrative of Toy Story
4 seems to be centered on Forky, voiced by

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:43.899
Tony Hale, who seems to be in the midst of
an existential crisis about whether or not

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:44.880
he's truly a toy.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.809
Jordan Peele and Keegan-Michael Key also join
the film as Bunny and Ducky, a pair of stuffed

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:54.120
animals who join forces with Woody and friends,
while Christina Hendricks will join the cast

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.379
as a character named Gabby Gabby, a vintage
baby doll who commands an army of ventriloquist

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.060
dummies in an antique mall, and appears to
be the central villain of the film.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.740
The extra wait for Toy Story 4 may have been
frustrating for fans, but it helped the timing

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.700
align in at least one crucial way: Keanu Reeves'
voice work as new character Duke Caboom arrives

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.380
in the midst of a career revival for the Hollywood
veteran.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.220
It's just another reminder that Reeves can
handle pretty much any type of role and as

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.860
the Pixar brass discovered shortly after arranging
a meeting, he gives his all to any character,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.400
even the ones made out of plastic.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.820
Director Josh Cooley told Entertainment Weekly:

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.780
"Once Keanu came to the table, he was just
asking all of these great questions about

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:31.500
the character.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.600
It made us realize that we weren't digging
deep enough for this character and there's

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.060
a real opportunity to have him support Woody's
story in a much bigger way."

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.680
Reeves revealed that digging deeper included
building out a touching backstory for Duke,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.720
a Canadian stuntman sold to kids with promises
the toy might not have been able to fulfill.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.120
"He's the most spectacular daredevil Canada
has ever seen"

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:55.820
Reeves explained:

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.020
"Duke let his kid down when he couldn't do
what the commercial said he could.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.460
So he's a wounded person!

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.600
[...] I wanted him to have a real sensitivity
and a soft heart."

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:08.580
You may have noticed one surprising returning
cast member of Toy Story 4: Don Rickles, the

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.920
voice of Mr. Potato Head.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.880
Not that Rickles' performance needed changing
he's one of the most entertaining side characters

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:14.800
in the franchise.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.820
"You would not believe what I've been through
tonight."

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:25.480
However, Rickles died in 2017 as the script
for the film was still being written.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:29.870
He'd signed on to be a part of it, but was
unable to record any lines for the new film.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.659
After his passing, Rickles' family reached
out to Pixar and asked if there was any way

00:02:33.659 --> 00:02:35.980
that the late comedian could still be a part
of the film.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.730
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
director Josh Cooley confirmed that there

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.980
was plenty of material to bring Rickles back
for one more go, saying:

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:48.640
"We went through, jeez, 25 years of everything
we didn't use for Toy Story 1, 2, 3, the theme

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.160
parks, the ice capades, the video games — everything
that he's recorded for Mr. Potato Head.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.439
[...] And so I'm very honored that they asked
us to do that, and I'm very honored that he's

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.060
in the film.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.320
Nobody can replace him."

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.620
At the end of Toy Story 3, Andy decided it
was time to move on from his childhood toys

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.400
and passed them along to Bonnie, inducing
tears for about the fifth time during the

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:07.900
film.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:11.760
Toy Story 4 will reportedly pick up with what
sounds like a flashback to a time between

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.240
the events of Toy Story 2 and Toy Story 3
-- a time when Bo Peep was still around.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.760
If you recall, she was absent without much
explanation in the third film.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.739
"Yeah, we've lost friends along the way.

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:25.260
Wheezy, and Etch, and…

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:25.920
Bo Peep?

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.000
Yeah, even Bo."

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.540
Those who have seen the beginning of Toy Story
4 indicate that it will fill in many blanks

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.659
about where Bo Peep disappeared to and what
Woody, Buzz, and the rest of the toys have

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.200
been up to since we last saw them.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.500
MovieWeb writes that the main events of the
film take place nine years after the first

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.760
scene, bringing us back to the main events
with Woody and the gang adjusting to their

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.900
new life with Bonnie.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.460
Toy Story 4 has been in the works for quite
some time, and not just due to the fact that

00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:57.499
Pixar's animation process and attention to
detail takes a long time to complete.

00:03:57.499 --> 00:04:01.200
The film has actually gone through a series
of writing and directing changes since it

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.020
was first announced in 2014.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.060
The original directing duo was cut in half
when John Lasseter stepped down, but that's

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.220
just one of several behind-the-scenes shake-ups.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.529
The film has also been through a number of
writers, and even saw a near-total rewrite

00:04:13.529 --> 00:04:14.060
at one point.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:18.140
Rashida Jones and Will McCormack were originally
in charge of the story, but they walked away

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.360
about the same time Lasseter stepped down
from his role as the co-director.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.160
It's too bad for Pixar that the delays pushed
back Toy Story 4 so far, but we did get the

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.280
delightful Incredibles 2 to fill the space.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.620
Not a terrible second choice.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.360
In the original version of the script, Toy
Story 4 was billed as a romantic comedy.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:39.580
Pixar president Jim Morris told Disney Latino
in 2015 that Toy Story 4 would still follow

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:43.710
the arc established by previous chapters in
the franchise, but it would also follow its

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.160
own path and tell a totally different type
of story.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.800
According to Morris, that the film won't focus
much on the relationship between toys and

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.320
children, but would instead depict a love
story between Woody and Bo Peep.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.480
This may be an indication of why the studio
reached out to Jones and McCormack, who had

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.820
previously written the film Celeste and Jesse
Forever.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.250
However, in the interim, the script has gone
through some major changes since it was originally

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.381
conceived, and it seems possible that Toy
Story 4 may have reverted back to some of

00:05:08.381 --> 00:05:11.280
the more familiar storytelling beats the series
is known for.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:15.100
"Jesse Ham Bo Rex Potato Head Hey watch it
Pal…”

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.480
“Where do we go?”

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.820
“Let’s go save a spork."

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.700
Considering that Toy Story 3 seemed to wrap
up the franchise on a perfect note, many fans

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.390
were surprised to hear that Pixar was making
a fourth film.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.770
It might be hard to believe there's another
great story to tell here, but according to

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:32.480
the film's stars, Toy Story 4 is the most
emotional chapter in the series.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:36.400
Tim Allen, who plays Buzz Lightyear, appeared
on The Talk and told the hosts that he actually

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.540
struggled to get through the final scenes
of Toy Story 4 due to their emotional weight.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.920
"I gotta resist getting emotional.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.620
I don't want to give it away, but this is
an incredibly great story."

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:50.360
Tom Hanks, who voices Woody, echoed those
sentiments, telling The Chris Evans Show that

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.420
he could barely even read his lines on the
last day.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:57.100
"When I went in for my last day of recording,
I wanted to have my back to them."

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:01.620
"I didn't want to see them and I wanted to
pretend they couldn't see me."

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.540
It could be easy to dismiss Hanks and Allen's
comments they're hyping their upcoming film,

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.620
after all, and they've played these characters
since 1995.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.140
Of course it was emotional for them.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.480
However, the response to an early screening
of Toy Story 4's opening act seems to indicate

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:19.150
that this is more than just a couple of big
stars trying to put butts in seats.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.920
In April 2019, Disney surprised the audience
at CinemaCon by showing the first 17 minutes

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:27.490
of the film, and it sounds like Hanks and
Allen aren't just paying lip service with

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.160
their comments.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:32.180
Essentially, it sounds like you may need to
see Toy Story 4 more than once, as you might

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.960
be crying too much the first time around to
catch every detail.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.240
"I can't watch!

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:37.920
Can someone cover my eyes?"

